From 3b5cbd5672395e869853cc35fa5b9987cb3ea30e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: locatemayank <locatemayank@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:50:24 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Rework letter recognition and touch handling for small
 fingers

Recognition
- Replace target-biased template match (accepted any 18px of ink) with a
  tracing-coverage check: finger-sized guide dots, per-stroke coverage,
  precision, direction alignment and ink-length limits.
- Add $P point-cloud fallback for letters drawn freehand off the guide,
  with scribble rejection and lookalike-group leniency.
- Kind verdicts: pass / almost (missing dots glow pink) / other letter /
  scribble or retry (wipe + stroke-order animation). Leniency grows after
  each "almost" so no child gets stuck.

Touch
- New touch arbiter: one finger draws even with a hand resting on the
  screen; two fingers together, pinches, palms and edge grips are
  rejected; stylus wins over touch; no more stuck-pointer state.
- Taps leave a dot, short strokes count, coalesced events, clamped
  points, lostpointercapture keeps the stroke.
- Offscreen ink cache + rAF rendering instead of shadowBlur redraws.
- Block long-press menus, selection, double-tap/pinch zoom, pull-to-refresh.

Game flow
- Green numbered start dot + arrow, dots light up gold while tracing,
  spoken "Can you trace B?", "Done" button, auto-pass on completion.
- Locked celebration phase (fixes double reveal skipping a letter).
- Ink is remapped on resize/rotation instead of drifting off the guide.
- Remove stray <![CDATA[ ... ]]> wrapper around index.html that hid the
  doctype (page was rendering in quirks mode).

Service worker v17: network-first for the page so updates show on the
next launch; never cache error responses.

Sources and tests live in tests/ (see tests/README.md).
