@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+# Magic Letter Zoo – sources and tests
+
+`index.html` at the repo root is the shipped game (single file, no build step needed to deploy).
+The script inside it is assembled from the files here:
+
+| File | What it is |
+|---|---|
+| `engine.js` | `LetterEngine`: letter stroke templates, guide-dot layout, tracing-coverage check, $P free-draw recognizer, final verdict (pass / almost / other / scribble / retry) |
+| `arbiter.js` | `createTouchArbiter`: decides which touch may draw (one finger draws; resting hand doesn't block; two-finger, pinch, palm and edge-grip touches rejected; stylus wins) |
+| `game.js` | Game controller: canvas rendering, pointer wiring, guide dots, voice, animals, celebration flow |
+| `build.py` | Rebuilds the `<script>` block in `../index.html` from the three files above and syntax-checks it |
+
+## Workflow
+
+```
+# edit engine.js / arbiter.js / game.js, then:
+python tests/build.py
+cd tests
+node test_arbiter.js     # 17 touch scenarios
+node sim.js              # simulated preschool handwriting (env: N, W, H, LEN)
+node smoke_dom.js        # headless walk-through of ../index.html with stubbed DOM
+```
+
+`ENGINE=./orig_engine.js node sim.js` runs the same simulation against the previous recognizer
+(baseline). Results at 640×520, 780 attempts per row:
+
+| Scenario | Previous | Current |
+|---|---|---|
+| Good trace → pass | 100% | 99.6% |
+| Sloppy trace → pass | 100% | 97.2% |
+| Missing stroke → not passed | 42% | 92.3% |
+| Half traced → not passed | 0% | 99.4% |
+| Zig-zag scribble → not passed | 0% | 95.5% |
+| Loop scribble → not passed | 0% | 100% |
+| Random scribble → not passed | 0% | 99.1% |
+| Wrong letter on guide → not passed | 0% | 91.3% |
+| Free-drawn target off guide → pass | 100% | 96.5% |
